;; The closed-world image analysis: which image objects the program can reach as values, and which

;; of their properties it can store to. Its results are the tables of `aot.facts`; its consumers
;; are the PropAccess fold on a StaticRef owner (`aot.node.property`) and the [[Prototype]] Load
;; fold on a StaticRef pointer (`aot.node.memory`). docs/COMPILE-TIME.md §8 row 10.
;;
;; ## The question
;;
;; A read `X.K` of an image object X folds to the image word when no store in the program can have
;; written K on X. The image is data; the program is every graph in the arena once the world is
;; closed (every source function lowered, every JSL definition that any of them demands built).
;; So the question is answered by one walk over every node of every graph, run to a fixpoint.
;;
;; ## The abstraction
;;
;; Every value-carrying node has an abstract value: the SET of image entries it may denote, plus
;; TOP — "possibly an object the analysis does not name": a fresh allocation, a parameter, a call
;; result, a property read that a store may have overwritten. The unnamed objects are, by
;; induction, exactly the escaped image objects and the non-image objects, which is what makes
;; the two tables close over each other:
;;
;;   - a node's value ESCAPES when it reaches an input position the transfer below does not
;;     follow: a call argument, a return value, a stored value, a thrown value, an array element,
;;     an unknown primitive's operand. Its named entries become `escaped`.
;;   - a STORE names its owner. Owner named as X: `written(X, K)`. Owner TOP: the key K joins the
;;     unknown-owner keys, which count as written on every escaped entry. A runtime key: the same
;;     with "any key".
;;
;; The transfer, per node:
;;
;;   StaticRef X (object or function)    {X}
;;   Box, Unbox, Cast, Phi               the inputs' values, united
;;   Proj of a PropLoad, value           the owner's K-word (an object REF adds its entry; a
;;                                       written pair adds TOP); TOP owner: the K-word of every
;;                                       escaped entry, and TOP
;;   Proj of JS-PROP-GET-OWN, value      as above; a runtime key reads every REF word
;;   Load of the [[Prototype]] word      the owner's prototype; TOP owner: every entry any object
;;                                       may have as a prototype (P below), and TOP once a
;;                                       prototype store exists
;;   Load of the properties word         the owner's set, flagged STORAGE (a backing store, not
;;                                       an object)
;;   Load of a property alias            from a STORAGE value: the owner's word for the alias's
;;                                       key, as for PropLoad
;;   Parm, call result, anything else    TOP
;;
;; P, the prototypes a fresh or unnamed object may carry, is every entry that is some image entry's
;; prototype word together with every registered intrinsic (`heap-intrinsic-entry-at`): a fresh
;; ordinary object sits on %Object.prototype%, a function on %Function.prototype%, an array on
;; %Array.prototype%, each of which the realm layout registers.
;;
;; The tables only grow, the abstraction is finite, and every rule is monotone in the tables, so
;; iterating the walk until nothing changes reaches the least fixpoint, which is a sound
;; over-approximation of what the program can do.
;;
;; ## Why the answer survives optimization
;;
;; The pass runs before Opto; inlining then replaces a callee's Parm with the actual argument, so
;; a store whose owner the analysis saw as TOP becomes a store on a named entry, and a read that
;; was on a Parm becomes a read on a StaticRef that the fold answers. Both are covered: the
;; argument reached a call input, so its entries are escaped, and the store's key was recorded
;; against unknown owners — `written` is already true for that pair. A callee's Return value
;; reached a return position, so its entries are escaped before the caller ever sees them
;; inlined. Folds replace nodes with constants the analysis already accounted for. What would
;; break the answer is a graph the analysis never saw: a JSL definition built after it ran
;; (`jsl-build-graph!` refuses), or an image entry added after it ran (`aot.facts` refuses).
;;
;; ## Calls
;;
;; The call graph is closed and finite, so values flow through it instead of escaping at it. A
;; Parm is a Phi over its Fun's callers (aot.node.call): its value is the union of the matching
;; argument at every linked Call. A Call the pessimistic pass has not linked yet — a value call,
;; whose code-word Load is typed as the finite set of every function the realm lowered, linked by
;; SCCP during Opto — is simulated here: each argument flows into the matching Parm of every
;; function the set names, and the call's value is the union of those functions' Return values,
;; exactly the edges Opto will add. A Return's value therefore reaches only its callers' result
;; projections; it escapes only from a function with the external caller hook (the entry
;; wrapper). A call whose pointer type names no finite set is the one place arguments still
;; escape and the result is TOP. This is why `JsGetNamedObject`, which takes every prototype it
;; visits as an argument and only reads it, escapes none of them.
;;
;; ## What is not here yet
;;
;; `delete` and Object.defineProperty are not lowered today (each is a refusal). When they land
;; they are stores in this analysis' sense — a delete changes an image shape, an accessor changes
;; what a read means — and must mark the pair they touch, or the owner's every key.
;;
;; Simple has no counterpart: its heap begins empty. This is the JavaScript divergence written
;; down in docs/DECISIONS.md (image object property reads fold under closed-world facts).
(module aot.node.imagefacts)
(import "coil.primitive" :as primitive)
(import "coil.alloc" :as alloc)
(import "coil.arraylist" :use *)
(import "coil.os" :as os)
(import "aot.util.panic" :use *)
(import "aot.node.node" :use *)
(import "aot.node.control" :use *)
(import "aot.node.dynamic" :use *)
(import "aot.node.memory" :use *)
(import "aot.node.property" :use *)
(import "aot.node.call" :use *)
(import "aot.node.jsops" :use *)
(import "aot.heap" :use *)
(import "aot.shape" :use *)
(import "aot.facts" :use *)
(import "aot.type.type" :use *)

(defstruct ImageScan
  [(trace bool)  ; `AOT_FACTS_TRACE=1` narrates each escape and each named store
   (top (ArrayList bool))  ; per nid
   (storage (ArrayList bool))  ; per nid: the value is an object's backing store
   (set-id (ArrayList i64))  ; per nid: an index into `sets`, or -1
   (sets (ArrayList (ArrayList i64)))
   (protos (ArrayList i64))  ; P
   (changed bool)
   (rounds i64)])

(defn imagescan [] (-> (ptr ImageScan))
  (primitive/alloc-static ImageScan))

(defn scan--reset! [(node-count i64)] (-> i64)
  (let [s (imagescan)
        a (alloc/malloc-allocator)
        (mut i) 0]
    (set! (.top s) (al-new [bool] a))
    (set! (.storage s) (al-new [bool] a))
    (set! (.set-id s) (al-new [i64] a))
    (set! (.sets s) (al-new [(ArrayList i64)] a))
    (set! (.protos s) (al-new [i64] a))
    (set! (.changed s) false)
    (set! (.rounds s) 0)
    (set! (.trace s) (!= (primitive/cast i64 (os/getenv c"AOT_FACTS_TRACE")) 0))
    (loop (if (> (load i) node-count)
              (break 0)
              (do
                (push! [bool] (mut (.top s)) false)
                (push! [bool] (mut (.storage s)) false)
                (push! [i64] (mut (.set-id s)) -1)
                (set! (mut i) (+ (load i) 1))
                (continue))))))

(defn scan--note! [(changed bool)] (-> i64)
  (do (if changed (set! (.changed (imagescan)) true) 0) 0))

(defn scan--top? [(nid i64)] (-> bool)
  (get (.top (imagescan)) nid))

(defn scan--storage? [(nid i64)] (-> bool)
  (get (.storage (imagescan)) nid))

(defn scan--set-top! [(nid i64)] (-> i64)
  (let [s (imagescan)]
    (if (get (.top s) nid)
        0
        (do (set! (mut (.top s)) nid true) (scan--note! true)))))

(defn scan--set-storage! [(nid i64)] (-> i64)
  (let [s (imagescan)]
    (if (get (.storage s) nid)
        0
        (do (set! (mut (.storage s)) nid true) (scan--note! true)))))

(defn scan--count [(nid i64)] (-> i64)
  (let [s (imagescan)
        id (get (.set-id s) nid)]
    (if (< id 0) 0 (len (get (.sets s) id)))))

(defn scan--entry-at [(nid i64) (i i64)] (-> i64)
  (let [s (imagescan)]
    (get (get (.sets s) (get (.set-id s) nid)) i)))

(defn scan--has? [(nid i64) (entry i64)] (-> bool)
  (let [n (scan--count nid)
        (mut i) 0
        (mut found) false]
    (loop (if (or (load found) (>= (load i) n))
              (break (load found))
              (do
                (if (= (scan--entry-at nid (load i)) entry)
                    (set! (mut found) true)
                    0)
                (set! (mut i) (+ (load i) 1))
                (continue))))))

(defn scan--add! [(nid i64) (entry i64)] (-> i64)
  (let [s (imagescan)]
    (if (< entry 0)
        (panic-i "imagefacts: adding a non-entry to a value set" entry)
        0)
    (if (scan--has? nid entry)
        0
        (do
          (if (< (get (.set-id s) nid) 0)
              (do
                (set! (mut (.set-id s)) nid (len (.sets s)))
                (push! [(ArrayList i64)]
                       (mut (.sets s))
                       (al-new [i64] (alloc/malloc-allocator))))
              0)
          (push! [i64]
                 (mut (al-elem [(ArrayList i64)]
                               (mut (.sets s))
                               (get (.set-id s) nid)))
                 entry)
          (scan--note! true)))))

;; `dst` denotes at least what `src` denotes.
(defn scan--copy-into! [(dst i64) (src i64)] (-> i64)
  (let [n (scan--count src)
        (mut i) 0]
    (if (scan--top? src) (scan--set-top! dst) 0)
    (if (scan--storage? src) (scan--set-storage! dst) 0)
    (loop (if (>= (load i) n)
              (break 0)
              (do
                (scan--add! dst (scan--entry-at src (load i)))
                (set! (mut i) (+ (load i) 1))
                (continue))))))

;; The value at `nid` reached a position the transfer does not follow.
(defn scan--escape! [(nid i64)] (-> i64)
  (let [n (scan--count nid)
        (mut i) 0]
    (loop (if (>= (load i) n)
              (break 0)
              (do
                (if (scan--storage? nid)
                    ;; A backing store handed out whole: any of its words may change.
                    (scan--note! (facts-mark-any-key! (scan--entry-at nid
                                                                      (load i))))
                    (if (facts-mark-escaped! (scan--entry-at nid (load i)))
                        (do
                          (if (.trace (imagescan))
                              (match (arena-node nid)
                                (Some [v]
                                      (do
                                        (println "imagefacts: entry {} escapes as {s}"
                                                 (scan--entry-at nid (load i))
                                                 (n-text v))
                                        0))
                                (None [] 0))
                              0)
                          (scan--note! true))
                        0))
                (set! (mut i) (+ (load i) 1))
                (continue))))))

(defn scan--escape-node! [(n (dyn NodeOps))] (-> i64)
  (scan--escape! (n-nid n)))

;; The value at `v` escapes at input `i` of `user`; narrated under the trace flag when it names
;; an entry not yet escaped.
(defn scan--escape-at! [(user (dyn NodeOps)) (i i64) (v (dyn NodeOps))] (-> i64)
  (do
    (if (and (.trace (imagescan)) (> (scan--count (n-nid v)) 0))
        (let [k (scan--count (n-nid v))
              (mut j) 0]
          (loop (if (>= (load j) k)
                    (break 0)
                    (do
                      (if (facts-escaped? (scan--entry-at (n-nid v) (load j)))
                          0
                          (do
                            (println "imagefacts:   at input {} of {s}"
                                     i
                                     (n-text user))
                            0))
                      (set! (mut j) (+ (load j) 1))
                      (continue)))))
        0)
    (scan--escape-node! v)))

(defn scan--escape-inputs-from! [(n (dyn NodeOps)) (first i64)] (-> i64)
  (let [(mut i) first]
    (loop (if (>= (load i) (n-nins n))
              (break 0)
              (do
                (match (n-in n (load i))
                  (Some [v] (scan--escape-at! n (load i) v))
                  (None [] 0))
                (set! (mut i) (+ (load i) 1))
                (continue))))))

;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; Image words
;; An entry the abstraction names: an object, never a string or a backing store (whose words are
;; property values, not a prototype and a properties word).
(defn scan--object-entry? [(entry i64)] (-> bool)
  (and (>= entry 0) (heap-entry-object? entry)))

;; The index of X's own property `key` in its backing store, or -1.
(defn scan--own-index [(entry i64) (key i64)] (-> i64)
  (let [storage (heap-entry-storage entry)]
    (if (< storage 0)
        -1
        (let [shape (heap-entry-shape storage)]
          (if (shape-has-key? shape key)
              (/ (shape-offset-key shape key) HEAP-WORD-BYTES)
              -1)))))

;; The value read as `X.K` (own step only): the image word's entry, and TOP when a store may have
;; replaced it.
(defn scan--add-own-word-into! [(nid i64) (entry i64) (key i64)] (-> i64)
  (do
    (if (facts-written? entry key) (scan--set-top! nid) 0)
    (let [k (scan--own-index entry key)]
      (if (< k 0)
          0
          (let [storage (heap-entry-storage entry)
                target
                  (image-word-object-entry (heap-entry-word storage k)
                                           (heap-entry-word-kind storage k))]
            (if (>= target 0) (scan--add! nid target) 0))))))

;; Every REF word of X's backing store, and TOP: a read whose key is a runtime value.
(defn scan--add-all-words-into! [(nid i64) (entry i64)] (-> i64)
  (let [storage (heap-entry-storage entry)]
    (scan--set-top! nid)
    (if (< storage 0)
        0
        (let [n (heap-entry-word-count storage)
              (mut k) 0]
          (loop (if (>= (load k) n)
                    (break 0)
                    (let [target
                            (image-word-object-entry (heap-entry-word storage
                                                                      (load k))
                                                     (heap-entry-word-kind storage
                                                                           (load k)))]
                      (if (>= target 0) (scan--add! nid target) 0)
                      (set! (mut k) (+ (load k) 1))
                      (continue))))))))

;; A read on an owner the analysis does not name: the word of every escaped entry.
(defn scan--add-escaped-words-into! [(nid i64) (key i64)] (-> i64)
  (let [n (heap-count)
        (mut e) 0]
    (scan--set-top! nid)
    (loop (if (>= (load e) n)
              (break 0)
              (do
                (if (and (scan--object-entry? (load e))
                         (facts-escaped? (load e)))
                    (if (< key 0)
                        (scan--add-all-words-into! nid (load e))
                        (scan--add-own-word-into! nid (load e) key))
                    0)
                (set! (mut e) (+ (load e) 1))
                (continue))))))

(defn scan--add-prototype-into! [(nid i64) (entry i64)] (-> i64)
  (let [target
          (image-word-object-entry (heap-entry-word entry
                                                    HEAP-OFFSET-PROTOTYPE-WORD)
                                   (heap-entry-word-kind entry
                                                         HEAP-OFFSET-PROTOTYPE-WORD))]
    (if (facts-prototypes-written?) (scan--set-top! nid) 0)
    (if (>= target 0) (scan--add! nid target) 0)))

(defn scan--add-all-prototypes-into! [(nid i64)] (-> i64)
  (let [s (imagescan)
        n (len (.protos s))
        (mut i) 0]
    (scan--set-top! nid)
    (loop (if (>= (load i) n)
              (break 0)
              (do
                (scan--add! nid (get (.protos s) (load i)))
                (set! (mut i) (+ (load i) 1))
                (continue))))))

(defn scan--protos-push! [(entry i64)] (-> i64)
  (let [s (imagescan)
        n (len (.protos s))
        (mut i) 0
        (mut found) false]
    (loop (if (or (load found) (>= (load i) n))
              (break 0)
              (do
                (if (= (get (.protos s) (load i)) entry)
                    (set! (mut found) true)
                    0)
                (set! (mut i) (+ (load i) 1))
                (continue))))
    (if (load found) 0 (do (push! [i64] (mut (.protos s)) entry) 0))))

;; P: every entry that is some entry's prototype, and every registered intrinsic.
(defn scan--compute-protos! [] (-> i64)
  (let [n (heap-count)
        (mut e) 0]
    (loop (if (>= (load e) n)
              (break 0)
              (do
                (if (scan--object-entry? (load e))
                    (let [target
                            (image-word-object-entry (heap-entry-word (load e)
                                                                      HEAP-OFFSET-PROTOTYPE-WORD)
                                                     (heap-entry-word-kind (load e)
                                                                           HEAP-OFFSET-PROTOTYPE-WORD))]
                      (if (>= target 0) (scan--protos-push! target) 0))
                    0)
                (set! (mut e) (+ (load e) 1))
                (continue))))
    (let [k (heap-intrinsic-count)
          (mut i) 0]
      (loop (if (>= (load i) k)
                (break 0)
                (do
                  (scan--protos-push! (heap-intrinsic-entry-at (load i)))
                  (set! (mut i) (+ (load i) 1))
                  (continue)))))))

;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; The transfer

;; A property read `owner.key` (own step) into `nid`; key -1 is a runtime key.
(defn scan--read-into! [(nid i64) (owner i64) (key i64)] (-> i64)
  (let [n (scan--count owner)
        (mut i) 0]
    (if (scan--top? owner) (scan--add-escaped-words-into! nid key) 0)
    (loop (if (>= (load i) n)
              (break 0)
              (do
                (if (< key 0)
                    (scan--add-all-words-into! nid
                                               (scan--entry-at owner (load i)))
                    (scan--add-own-word-into! nid
                                              (scan--entry-at owner (load i))
                                              key))
                (set! (mut i) (+ (load i) 1))
                (continue))))))

;; A read of `key` that may continue up the prototype chain: the owner's own word, and the word of
;; every prototype in the program (the chain of an unknown owner is any of them).
(defn scan--read-chain-into! [(nid i64) (owner i64) (key i64)] (-> i64)
  (let [s (imagescan)
        n (len (.protos s))
        (mut i) 0]
    (scan--read-into! nid owner key)
    (loop (if (>= (load i) n)
              (break 0)
              (do
                (if (< key 0)
                    (scan--add-all-words-into! nid (get (.protos s) (load i)))
                    (scan--add-own-word-into! nid
                                              (get (.protos s) (load i))
                                              key))
                (set! (mut i) (+ (load i) 1))
                (continue))))))

;; A store of `key` on `owner`; key -1 is a runtime key.
(defn scan--write! [(owner i64) (key i64)] (-> i64)
  (let [n (scan--count owner)
        (mut i) 0]
    (if (and (.trace (imagescan)) (or (> n 0) (scan--top? owner)))
        (match (arena-node owner)
          (Some [o]
                (do
                  (println "imagefacts: store of key {} on {s} (top {}, {} named)"
                           key
                           (n-text o)
                           (scan--top? owner)
                           n)
                  0))
          (None [] 0))
        0)
    (if (scan--top? owner)
        (scan--note! (if (< key 0)
                         (facts-mark-unknown-owner-any!)
                         (facts-mark-unknown-owner-key! key)))
        0)
    (loop (if (>= (load i) n)
              (break 0)
              (do
                (scan--note! (if (< key 0)
                                 (facts-mark-any-key! (scan--entry-at owner
                                                                      (load i)))
                                 (facts-mark-written! (scan--entry-at owner
                                                                      (load i))
                                                      key)))
                (set! (mut i) (+ (load i) 1))
                (continue))))))

;; A jsop key operand: the interned key when constant, else -1.
(defn scan--key-operand [(k (dyn NodeOps))] (-> i64)
  (let [t (n-ty k)]
    (if (and (ty-int? t) (ty-constant? t)) (ty-int-lo t) -1)))

(defn scan--value-proj! [(nid i64) (multi (dyn NodeOps)) (idx i64)] (-> i64)
  (let [op (n-op multi)]
    (if (or (= op OP-PROPLOAD) (= op OP-PROPSTORE))
        (if (!= idx PROP-RESULT-VALUE)
            0
            (if (= (prop-access-kind multi) PROP-LOAD)
                (scan--read-into! nid
                                  (n-nid (n-in! multi PROP-OBJECT))
                                  (prop-access-key multi))
                (if (= (prop-access-kind multi) PROP-STORE)
                    (scan--copy-into! nid (n-nid (n-in! multi PROP-VALUE)))
                    ;; The holder of a key is some prototype along the chain, or null.
                    (if (= (prop-access-kind multi) PROP-HOLDER)
                        (scan--add-all-prototypes-into! nid)
                        ;; [[Get]] reads the key on the owner or on some prototype; the fast Set
                        ;; answers the value it stored.
                        (if (= (prop-access-kind multi) PROP-GET)
                            (scan--read-chain-into! nid
                                                    (n-nid (n-in! multi
                                                                  PROP-OBJECT))
                                                    (prop-access-key multi))
                            (if (= (prop-access-kind multi) PROP-SET)
                                (scan--copy-into! nid
                                                  (n-nid (n-in! multi
                                                                PROP-VALUE)))
                                0))))))
        (if (= op OP-JSOP)
            (let [prim (jsop-prim multi)]
              (if (!= idx 2)
                  0
                  (if (= prim JS-PROP-GET-OWN)
                      (scan--read-into! nid
                                        (n-nid (n-in! multi JSOP-ARG0))
                                        (scan--key-operand (n-in! multi
                                                                  (+ JSOP-ARG0
                                                                     1))))
                      (if (= prim JS-PROP-GET)
                          (scan--read-chain-into! nid
                                                  (n-nid (n-in! multi JSOP-ARG0))
                                                  (scan--key-operand (n-in! multi
                                                                            (+ JSOP-ARG0
                                                                               1))))
                          (if (= prim JS-PROP-SET)
                              (scan--copy-into! nid
                                                (n-nid (n-in! multi
                                                              (+ JSOP-ARG0 2))))
                              (if (= prim JS-PROP-CHAIN-HOLDER)
                                  (scan--add-all-prototypes-into! nid)
                                  (if (= prim JS-GET-PROTOTYPE)
                                      (let [owner
                                              (n-nid (n-in! multi JSOP-ARG0))
                                            n (scan--count owner)
                                            (mut i) 0]
                                        (if (scan--top? owner)
                                            (scan--add-all-prototypes-into! nid)
                                            0)
                                        (loop (if (>= (load i) n)
                                                  (break 0)
                                                  (do
                                                    (scan--add-prototype-into! nid
                                                                               (scan--entry-at owner
                                                                                               (load i)))
                                                    (set! (mut i)
                                                          (+ (load i) 1))
                                                    (continue)))))
                                      ;; A primitive whose result is not a dyn or object word — a fresh array or
                                      ;; string, a number, a boolean — denotes no image object.
                                      (if (scan--jsop-object-result? prim)
                                          (scan--set-top! nid)
                                          0))))))))
            (if (= op OP-NEW)
                0
                (if (= op OP-CALLEND)
                    (if (= idx RETURN-VALUE)
                        (scan--call-result-into! nid (cend-call multi))
                        0)
                    (scan--set-top! nid)))))))

;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; Calls

;; The Funs a Call may reach: the linked Returns' owners, else the finite set its pointer's type
;; names. Empty means unknown.
(defn scan--call-targets [(c (dyn NodeOps))] (-> (ArrayList i64))
  (let [(mut funs) (al-new [i64] (alloc/malloc-allocator))]
    (match (call-cend c)
      (Some [e]
            (let [(mut i) 1]
              (loop (if (>= (load i) (n-nins e))
                        (break 0)
                        (do
                          (match (n-in e (load i))
                            (Some [ret]
                                  (match (return-fun ret)
                                    (Some [fun]
                                          (do
                                            (push! [i64] (mut funs) (n-nid fun))
                                            0))
                                    (None [] 0)))
                            (None [] 0))
                          (set! (mut i) (+ (load i) 1))
                          (continue))))))
      (None [] 0))
    (if (> (len (load funs)) 0)
        0
        (let [ft (n-ty (call-fptr c))]
          (if (and (ty-funptr? ft) (not (ty-funptr-high? ft)))
              (let [count (ty-funptr-target-count ft)
                    (mut i) 0]
                (loop (if (>= (load i) count)
                          (break 0)
                          (do
                            (match (arena-function (ty-funptr-target-at ft
                                                                        (load i)))
                              (Some [fun]
                                    (if (= (n-op fun) OP-FUN)
                                        (do
                                          (push! [i64] (mut funs) (n-nid fun))
                                          0)
                                        0))
                              (None [] 0))
                            (set! (mut i) (+ (load i) 1))
                            (continue)))))
              0)))
    (load funs)))

;; The value a call yields: the union of its targets' Return values.
(defn scan--call-result-into! [(nid i64) (c (dyn NodeOps))] (-> i64)
  (let [funs (scan--call-targets c)]
    (if (= (len funs) 0)
        (scan--set-top! nid)
        (al-for [fnid funs]
                (match (arena-node fnid)
                  (Some [fun]
                        (match (fun-ret fun)
                          (Some [ret]
                                (match (n-in ret RETURN-VALUE)
                                  (Some [v] (scan--copy-into! nid (n-nid v)))
                                  (None [] 0)))
                          (None [] 0)))
                  (None [] 0))))))

;; Each argument flows into the matching Parm of every target; with no known target, it escapes.
(defn scan--call-flow! [(c (dyn NodeOps))] (-> i64)
  (let [funs (scan--call-targets c)]
    (if (= (len funs) 0)
        (scan--escape-inputs-from! c CALL-ARG0)
        (al-for [fnid funs]
                (match (arena-node fnid)
                  (Some [fun]
                        (let [(mut o) 0]
                          (loop (if (>= (load o) (n-nouts fun))
                                    (break 0)
                                    (do
                                      (match (n-out fun (load o))
                                        (Some [p]
                                              (if (= (n-op p) OP-PARM)
                                                  (let [slot (parm-call-slot p)]
                                                    (if (and (>= slot CALL-ARG0)
                                                             (< slot
                                                                (- (n-nins c) 1)))
                                                        (scan--copy-into! (n-nid p)
                                                                          (n-nid (n-in! c
                                                                                        slot)))
                                                        0))
                                                  0))
                                        (None [] 0))
                                      (set! (mut o) (+ (load o) 1))
                                      (continue))))))
                  (None [] 0))))))

(defn scan--load! [(nid i64) (n (dyn NodeOps))] (-> i64)
  (let [alias (load-alias n)
        ptr_ (n-nid (n-in! n MEM-PTR))
        count (scan--count ptr_)]
    (if (= alias ALIAS-OBJECT-PROTOTYPE)
        (let [(mut i) 0]
          (if (scan--top? ptr_) (scan--add-all-prototypes-into! nid) 0)
          (loop (if (>= (load i) count)
                    (break 0)
                    (do
                      (scan--add-prototype-into! nid
                                                 (scan--entry-at ptr_ (load i)))
                      (set! (mut i) (+ (load i) 1))
                      (continue)))))
        (if (= alias ALIAS-OBJECT-PROPERTIES)
            (do (scan--copy-into! nid ptr_) (scan--set-storage! nid))
            (if (or (= alias ALIAS-OBJECT-SHAPE)
                    (= alias ALIAS-STRING-LENGTH)
                    (= alias ALIAS-STRING-DATA)
                    (= alias ALIAS-FUNCTION-CODE)
                    (= alias ALIAS-ARRAY-LENGTH))
                0
                (if (>= alias ALIAS-FIRST-PROPERTY)
                    (if (scan--storage? ptr_)
                        (scan--read-into! nid ptr_ (shape-alias-key-id alias))
                        (scan--set-top! nid))
                    (if (and (= alias ALIAS-BULK) (scan--storage? ptr_))
                        (scan--read-into! nid ptr_ -1)
                        (scan--set-top! nid))))))))

(defn scan--visit! [(n (dyn NodeOps))] (-> i64)
  (let [nid (n-nid n)
        op (n-op n)]
    (if (= op OP-STATICREF)
        (if (= (staticref-rep n) REP-STRING)
            0
            (scan--add! nid (staticref-entry n)))
        (if (or (= op OP-BOX) (= op OP-UNBOX) (= op OP-CAST))
            (scan--copy-into! nid (n-nid (n-in! n 1)))
            (if (or (= op OP-PHI) (= op OP-PARM))
                (let [(mut i) 1]
                  (loop (if (>= (load i) (n-nins n))
                            (break 0)
                            (do
                              (match (n-in n (load i))
                                (Some [v] (scan--copy-into! nid (n-nid v)))
                                (None [] 0))
                              (set! (mut i) (+ (load i) 1))
                              (continue)))))
                (if (= op OP-PROJ)
                    (scan--value-proj! nid (n-in! n 0) (proj-idx n))
                    (if (= op OP-LOAD)
                        (scan--load! nid n)
                        (if (or (= op OP-TYPETEST)
                                (= op OP-CON)
                                (= op OP-FUNPTR)
                                (= op OP-EQ)
                                (= op OP-NE)
                                (= op OP-LT)
                                (= op OP-LE)
                                (= op OP-ULT))
                            0
                            (scan--set-top! nid)))))))))

;; May this primitive's value result be an object the program already holds? Its declared result
;; type says: a dyn word may; a raw string or array pointer is a fresh allocation; anything else
;; is a number or a boolean.
(defn scan--jsop-object-result? [(prim i64)] (-> bool)
  (let [t (jsop-result-ty prim)]
    (or (ty-dyn? t) (= t (raw-object-ty)) (= t (raw-function-ty)))))

;; A jsop whose operands the analysis follows: reads of the object model, and pure predicates.
(defn scan--jsop-read? [(prim i64)] (-> bool)
  (or (= prim JS-PROP-GET-OWN)
      (= prim JS-PROP-HAS-OWN)
      (= prim JS-OBJECT-KEYS)
      (= prim JS-GET-PROTOTYPE)
      (= prim JS-PROP-ATTRIBUTES)
      (= prim JS-IS-EXTENSIBLE)
      (= prim JS-TEST-INTEGRITY)
      (= prim JS-PROP-CHAIN-HOLDER)
      (= prim JS-PROP-GET)
      ;; An array is never an image object; an element read yields TOP through the result rule.
      (= prim JS-ARRAY-LOAD)
      (= prim JS-ARRAY-HAS)
      (= prim JS-ARRAY-SET-LENGTH)
      (= prim JS-ARRAY-INDEX-OF-STRING)
      (= prim JS-IS-UNDEFINED)
      (= prim JS-IS-NULL)
      (= prim JS-IS-BOOL)
      (= prim JS-IS-INT)
      (= prim JS-IS-FLT)
      (= prim JS-IS-STRING)
      (= prim JS-IS-SYMBOL)
      (= prim JS-IS-OBJECT)
      (= prim JS-IS-ARRAY)
      (= prim JS-IS-FUNCTION)))

(defn scan--store-effects! [(n (dyn NodeOps))] (-> i64)
  (let [alias (mem-alias-of-node n)
        ptr_ (n-nid (n-in! n MEM-PTR))
        count (scan--count ptr_)]
    (scan--escape-node! (n-in! n STORE-VAL))
    (if (= alias ALIAS-OBJECT-PROTOTYPE)
        (if (or (scan--top? ptr_) (> count 0))
            (scan--note! (facts-mark-prototypes-written!))
            0)
        (if (>= alias ALIAS-FIRST-PROPERTY)
            (if (scan--storage? ptr_)
                (scan--write! ptr_ (shape-alias-key-id alias))
                (scan--write! ptr_ -1))
            (if (or (= alias ALIAS-OBJECT-PROPERTIES) (= alias ALIAS-BULK))
                (scan--write! ptr_ -1)
                0)))))

(defn scan--op-in? [(op i64) (ops (ArrayList i64))] (-> bool)
  (let [(mut i) 0
        (mut found) false]
    (loop (if (or (load found) (>= (load i) (len ops)))
              (break (load found))
              (do
                (if (= (get ops (load i)) op) (set! (mut found) true) 0)
                (set! (mut i) (+ (load i) 1))
                (continue))))))

;; Nodes whose operands the transfer follows or that carry no object operand at all: nothing they
;; do lets a value reach code the analysis does not see.
(defn scan--inert-ops [] (-> (ArrayList i64))
  (let [(mut ops) (al-new [i64] (alloc/malloc-allocator))]
    (push! [i64] (mut ops) OP-BOX)
    (push! [i64] (mut ops) OP-UNBOX)
    (push! [i64] (mut ops) OP-CAST)
    (push! [i64] (mut ops) OP-TYPETEST)
    (push! [i64] (mut ops) OP-PHI)
    (push! [i64] (mut ops) OP-PROJ)
    (push! [i64] (mut ops) OP-CPROJ)
    (push! [i64] (mut ops) OP-LOAD)
    (push! [i64] (mut ops) OP-CON)
    (push! [i64] (mut ops) OP-PARM)
    (push! [i64] (mut ops) OP-FUNPTR)
    (push! [i64] (mut ops) OP-IF)
    (push! [i64] (mut ops) OP-REGION)
    (push! [i64] (mut ops) OP-LOOP)
    (push! [i64] (mut ops) OP-START)
    (push! [i64] (mut ops) OP-STOP)
    (push! [i64] (mut ops) OP-FUN)
    (push! [i64] (mut ops) OP-MEMMERGE)
    (push! [i64] (mut ops) OP-MEMPHI)
    (push! [i64] (mut ops) OP-READONLY)
    (push! [i64] (mut ops) OP-NEW)
    (push! [i64] (mut ops) OP-EQ)
    (push! [i64] (mut ops) OP-NE)
    (push! [i64] (mut ops) OP-LT)
    (push! [i64] (mut ops) OP-LE)
    (push! [i64] (mut ops) OP-ULT)
    (push! [i64] (mut ops) OP-NOT)
    (push! [i64] (mut ops) OP-CALLEND)
    (push! [i64] (mut ops) OP-NEVER)
    (push! [i64] (mut ops) OP-XCTRL)
    (load ops)))

(defn scan--effects! [(n (dyn NodeOps)) (inert (ArrayList i64))] (-> i64)
  (let [op (n-op n)]
    (if (or (= op OP-PROPLOAD) (= op OP-PROPSTORE))
        (if (or (= (prop-access-kind n) PROP-STORE)
                (= (prop-access-kind n) PROP-SET))
            (do
              (scan--write! (n-nid (n-in! n PROP-OBJECT)) (prop-access-key n))
              (scan--escape-node! (n-in! n PROP-VALUE)))
            0)
        (if (= op OP-STORE)
            (scan--store-effects! n)
            (if (= op OP-CALL)
                (scan--call-flow! n)
                (if (= op OP-RETURN)
                    ;; The value reaches the callers' result projections; it leaves the analysed
                    ;; program only through the external caller hook.
                    (match (return-fun n)
                      (Some [fun]
                            (if (fun-unknown-callers? fun)
                                (scan--escape-inputs-from! n RETURN-VALUE)
                                0))
                      (None [] (scan--escape-inputs-from! n RETURN-VALUE)))
                    (if (= op OP-JSOP)
                        (let [prim (jsop-prim n)]
                          (if (or (= prim JS-PROP-SET-OWN)
                                  (= prim JS-PROP-SET-OWN-ATTRS)
                                  (= prim JS-PROP-SET)
                                  (= prim JS-PROP-DEFINE))
                              (do
                                (if (= prim JS-PROP-DEFINE)
                                    (scan--note! (facts-mark-descriptors!))
                                    0)
                                (scan--write! (n-nid (n-in! n JSOP-ARG0))
                                              (scan--key-operand (n-in! n
                                                                        (+ JSOP-ARG0
                                                                           1))))
                                (scan--escape-node! (n-in! n (+ JSOP-ARG0 2))))
                              ;; Freezing, sealing or closing an object changes every key's attributes: a write
                              ;; of every key, and descriptors exist.
                              (if (or (= prim JS-OBJECT-INTEGRITY)
                                      (= prim JS-PREVENT-EXTENSIONS))
                                  (do
                                    (scan--note! (facts-mark-descriptors!))
                                    (scan--write! (n-nid (n-in! n JSOP-ARG0))
                                                  -1))
                                  (if (= prim JS-ARRAY-STORE)
                                      ;; The element value escapes into the array; the array itself is read.
                                      (scan--escape-at! n
                                                        (+ JSOP-ARG0 2)
                                                        (n-in! n
                                                               (+ JSOP-ARG0 2)))
                                      (if (scan--jsop-read? prim)
                                          0
                                          (do
                                            (if (= prim JS-SET-PROTOTYPE)
                                                (scan--note! (facts-mark-prototypes-written!))
                                                0)
                                            (scan--escape-inputs-from! n
                                                                       JSOP-ARG0)))))))
                        (if (scan--op-in? op inert)
                            0
                            ;; Everything else hands its operands to code the analysis does not follow.
                            (scan--escape-inputs-from! n 0)))))))))

;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; The pass
(defn imagefacts-compute! [] (-> i64)
  (let [count (arena-node-count)
        s (imagescan)]
    (facts-begin! (heap-count) (shape-key-count))
    (scan--reset! count)
    (scan--compute-protos!)
    (let [inert (scan--inert-ops)]
      (loop (do
              (set! (.changed s) false)
              (set! (.rounds s) (+ (.rounds s) 1))
              (if (> (.rounds s) 10000)
                  (panic "imagefacts-compute!: the fixpoint did not converge")
                  0)
              (let [(mut i) 1]
                (loop (if (> (load i) count)
                          (break 0)
                          (do
                            (match (arena-node (load i))
                              (Some [n]
                                    (if (n-dead? n)
                                        0
                                        (do
                                          (scan--visit! n)
                                          (scan--effects! n inert))))
                              (None [] 0))
                            (set! (mut i) (+ (load i) 1))
                            (continue)))))
              (if (.changed s) (continue) (break 0)))))
    (facts-finish!)
    (if (.trace s)
        (let [n (heap-count)
              (mut e) 0]
          (loop (if (>= (load e) n)
                    (break 0)
                    (do
                      (if (scan--object-entry? (load e))
                          (do
                            (println "imagefacts: entry {} escaped {} any-key {}"
                                     (load e)
                                     (if (facts-escaped? (load e)) 1 0)
                                     (if (facts-any-key? (load e)) 1 0))
                            0)
                          0)
                      (set! (mut e) (+ (load e) 1))
                      (continue)))))
        0)
    (.rounds s)))

(defn imagefacts-rounds [] (-> i64)
  (.rounds (imagescan)))
